Choose the specific official page that supports the statement. Do not link to an unrelated homepage merely to satisfy a link requirement.

For other jurisdictions, use the appropriate government regulator, tax authority, central bank, or other authoritative source.

Requirements:

- Link to genuine, relevant sources.
- Use descriptive anchor text.
- Place references near the claims they support.
- Verify that the destination exists and supports the claim.
- Do not invent citations, statistics, reports, or source URLs.
- Do not add unnecessary outbound links just to reach a target number.
- External links should use normal crawlable HTML links.
- Open links in a new tab only when appropriate, and use safe rel attributes such as rel="noopener noreferrer" when applicable.

Do not automatically add nofollow to every trusted editorial reference. Use link attributes according to the actual relationship and purpose of the link.

If a financial claim cannot be verified, revise it, qualify it, or remove it.

## 15. FINANCIAL TRUST AND CONTENT SAFETY

Because the website covers money, accuracy and reader trust are essential.

